<!DOCTYPE refentry PUBLIC "-//OASIS//DTD DocBook XML V4.1.2//EN"
          "http://www.oasis-open.org/docbook/xml/4.1.2/docbookx.dtd">
<refentry id="process_extractemg">

	<refmeta>
		<refentrytitle>process_extractemg</refentrytitle>
		<manvolnum>1</manvolnum>
	</refmeta>

	<refnamediv>
		<refname>process_extractemg</refname>
		<refpurpose>identify, remove, and extract EMG events from a multichannel .dat using FastICA</refpurpose>
	</refnamediv>

	<refsynopsisdiv>
		<cmdsynopsis>
		<command>process_extractemg</command>
		<arg choice="plain"><option>-n</option> <replaceable>nChannels</replaceable></arg>
		<arg choice="plain"><option>-s</option> <replaceable>samplingRate</replaceable></arg>
		<arg choice="plain"><option>-c</option> <replaceable>groups</replaceable></arg>
		<arg><option>-w</option> <replaceable>nSamples</replaceable></arg>
		<arg><option>-p</option> <replaceable>peakIndex</replaceable></arg>
		<arg><option>-f</option> <replaceable>hpFreq</replaceable></arg>
		<arg><option>-t</option> <replaceable>thresholdFactor</replaceable></arg>
		<arg><option>-e</option> <replaceable>envelopeWindowMs</replaceable></arg>
		<arg><option>-r</option> <replaceable>refractory</replaceable></arg>
		<arg><option>-l</option> <replaceable>peakSearch</replaceable></arg>
		<arg><option>-d</option> <replaceable>downsample</replaceable></arg>
		<arg><option>-B</option> <replaceable>idStartSec</replaceable></arg>
		<arg><option>-Z</option> <replaceable>idDurationSec</replaceable></arg>
		<arg><option>-k</option> <replaceable>chunkSamples</replaceable></arg>
		<arg><option>--no-clean</option></arg>
		<arg><option>--no-emg-trace</option></arg>
		<arg><option>--no-waveforms</option></arg>
		<arg><option>-v</option></arg>
		<arg choice="plain"><replaceable>basename</replaceable></arg>
		</cmdsynopsis>
	</refsynopsisdiv>

	<refsect1>
		<title>Description</title>
		<para>
			<command>process_extractemg</command> identifies the
			electromyographic (EMG) component contaminating a
			multichannel extracellular recording, subtracts it from the
			raw signal to produce a cleaned <filename>.dat</filename>,
			and writes the EMG bursts as event files in the same format
			as spikes. It is a C++ port of the algorithmic core of the
			labbox MATLAB <literal>EMG_removing</literal> toolbox (Chen
			2019), restricted to the configuration the toolbox uses by
			default: deflation FastICA with the pow3 nonlinearity, run
			on high-pass filtered data, with the EMG component selected
			as the independent component whose channel loading is most
			spatially uniform.
		</para>
		<para>
			The implementation comes directly from the
			FastICA_25 toolbox shipped with labbox
			(<filename>fastica.m</filename>,
			<filename>fpica.m</filename>,
			<filename>whitenv.m</filename>,
			<filename>pcamat.m</filename>,
			<filename>remmean.m</filename>). Variable names in the
			C++ source mirror the MATLAB sources so the correspondence
			is auditable line-for-line. Only the deflation/pow3 path
			is ported; symmetric mode, tanh, gauss, skew nonlinearities,
			fine-tuning, stabilisation, and sample-size subsetting are
			not implemented because the EMG_removing toolbox does not
			use them.
		</para>
		<para>
			The pipeline runs in three passes:
		</para>
		<itemizedlist>
			<listitem>
				<para>
					<emphasis>Pass 1 (identification)</emphasis> reads
					<replaceable>idDurationSec</replaceable> seconds
					starting at <replaceable>idStartSec</replaceable>,
					removes the per-channel mean, applies a 4th-order
					Butterworth high-pass at
					<replaceable>hpFreq</replaceable>, downsamples by
					<replaceable>downsample</replaceable>, and runs
					FastICA. The EMG component is the IC maximising
					<literal>|sum(A[:,k] / ||A[:,k]||)|</literal> — the
					same diagnostic the MATLAB toolbox uses
					(<filename>EMG_rm_long.m</filename> line 259). The
					event-detection threshold is
					<literal>thresholdFactor · 1.4826 · MAD(|EMG_au|)</literal>
					evaluated on the un-filtered subsample.
				</para>
			</listitem>
			<listitem>
				<para>
					<emphasis>Pass 2 (streaming)</emphasis> reads the
					full <filename>.dat</filename> in chunks of
					<replaceable>chunkSamples</replaceable> samples per
					channel. For each sample <literal>t</literal>:
					<literal>EMG_au[t] = (raw[t,:] − μ) · Ws</literal>;
					the cleaned signal
					<literal>clean[t,c] = raw[t,c] − As[c]·EMG_au[t]</literal>
					is written to
					<filename>basename-emgclean.dat</filename> and
					<literal>EMG_au</literal> is written to
					<filename>basename.emg.&lt;g&gt;</filename>.
				</para>
			</listitem>
			<listitem>
				<para>
					<emphasis>Pass 3 (event extraction)</emphasis>
					smooths <literal>|EMG_au|</literal> with a boxcar
					of width <replaceable>envelopeWindowMs</replaceable>,
					finds threshold crossings separated by at least
					<replaceable>refractory</replaceable> samples,
					refines each peak inside a
					<replaceable>peakSearch</replaceable>-sample window,
					then mmaps the original
					<filename>.dat</filename> and copies a
					<replaceable>nSamples × nChannels(g)</replaceable>
					int16 waveform window into
					<filename>basename.spk.emg.&lt;g&gt;</filename>.
				</para>
			</listitem>
		</itemizedlist>
		<para>
			This tool is normally invoked through the
			<command>ndm_extractemg</command> pipeline script, which
			handles parameter file reading and multi-group looping.
		</para>
	</refsect1>

	<refsect1>
		<title>Required Arguments</title>
		<variablelist>
			<varlistentry>
				<term><option>-n</option> <replaceable>nChannels</replaceable></term>
				<listitem>
					<para>
						Total number of channels in the
						<filename>basename.dat</filename> file.
					</para>
				</listitem>
			</varlistentry>
			<varlistentry>
				<term><option>-s</option> <replaceable>samplingRate</replaceable></term>
				<listitem>
					<para>Sampling rate of the .dat in Hz.</para>
				</listitem>
			</varlistentry>
			<varlistentry>
				<term><option>-c</option> <replaceable>groups</replaceable></term>
				<listitem>
					<para>
						Channel groups: colon-separated list of
						comma-separated 0-based channel indices, e.g.
						<literal>0,1,2,3:8,9,10,11</literal> for two
						4-channel groups.
					</para>
				</listitem>
			</varlistentry>
			<varlistentry>
				<term><replaceable>basename</replaceable></term>
				<listitem>
					<para>Session basename without extension.</para>
				</listitem>
			</varlistentry>
		</variablelist>
	</refsect1>

	<refsect1>
		<title>Options</title>
		<variablelist>
			<varlistentry>
				<term><option>-w</option> <replaceable>W</replaceable></term>
				<listitem><para>Samples per event waveform (default 32).</para></listitem>
			</varlistentry>
			<varlistentry>
				<term><option>-p</option> <replaceable>P</replaceable></term>
				<listitem><para>Peak sample index within waveform (default 16).</para></listitem>
			</varlistentry>
			<varlistentry>
				<term><option>-f</option> <replaceable>F</replaceable></term>
				<listitem>
					<para>
						High-pass cutoff for FastICA component
						identification, in Hz (default 100). Raising
						this above the LFP band biases the leading IC
						towards the muscle component.
					</para>
				</listitem>
			</varlistentry>
			<varlistentry>
				<term><option>-t</option> <replaceable>T</replaceable></term>
				<listitem>
					<para>
						Event-detection threshold expressed as a
						multiple of <literal>1.4826·MAD(|EMG_au|)</literal>
						(default 5.0).
					</para>
				</listitem>
			</varlistentry>
			<varlistentry>
				<term><option>-e</option> <replaceable>MS</replaceable></term>
				<listitem>
					<para>
						Boxcar envelope smoothing window in milliseconds
						(default 20).
					</para>
				</listitem>
			</varlistentry>
			<varlistentry>
				<term><option>-r</option> <replaceable>R</replaceable></term>
				<listitem>
					<para>
						Minimum samples between consecutive accepted
						events (default 0 → derive from envelope window).
					</para>
				</listitem>
			</varlistentry>
			<varlistentry>
				<term><option>-l</option> <replaceable>L</replaceable></term>
				<listitem>
					<para>
						Samples after a threshold crossing within which
						the local maximum is found (default 0 → use
						refractory period).
					</para>
				</listitem>
			</varlistentry>
			<varlistentry>
				<term><option>-d</option> <replaceable>D</replaceable></term>
				<listitem>
					<para>
						Downsample factor for the identification pass
						(default 3). Larger values trade ID accuracy
						for memory + speed.
					</para>
				</listitem>
			</varlistentry>
			<varlistentry>
				<term><option>-B</option> <replaceable>S</replaceable></term>
				<listitem><para>ID-pass start time in seconds (default 0).</para></listitem>
			</varlistentry>
			<varlistentry>
				<term><option>-Z</option> <replaceable>S</replaceable></term>
				<listitem><para>ID-pass duration in seconds (default 60).</para></listitem>
			</varlistentry>
			<varlistentry>
				<term><option>-k</option> <replaceable>S</replaceable></term>
				<listitem>
					<para>
						Streaming chunk size for Pass 2, in samples
						per channel (default 1048576).
					</para>
				</listitem>
			</varlistentry>
			<varlistentry>
				<term><option>--no-clean</option></term>
				<listitem>
					<para>
						Skip writing
						<filename>basename-emgclean.dat</filename>.
					</para>
				</listitem>
			</varlistentry>
			<varlistentry>
				<term><option>--no-emg-trace</option></term>
				<listitem>
					<para>
						Skip writing per-group
						<filename>basename.emg.&lt;g&gt;</filename>.
					</para>
				</listitem>
			</varlistentry>
			<varlistentry>
				<term><option>--no-waveforms</option></term>
				<listitem>
					<para>
						Skip writing per-event waveform files
						<filename>basename.spk.emg.&lt;g&gt;</filename>.
					</para>
				</listitem>
			</varlistentry>
			<varlistentry>
				<term><option>-v</option></term>
				<listitem><para>Verbose progress output.</para></listitem>
			</varlistentry>
		</variablelist>
	</refsect1>

	<refsect1>
		<title>Output Files</title>
		<variablelist>
			<varlistentry>
				<term><filename>basename-emgclean.dat</filename></term>
				<listitem>
					<para>
						Same shape as
						<filename>basename.dat</filename> (int16,
						sample-major). For each group, the channels in
						that group have the EMG component subtracted.
						Channels not part of any group are passed
						through unchanged. The DC offset of the raw
						signal is preserved.
					</para>
				</listitem>
			</varlistentry>
			<varlistentry>
				<term><filename>basename.emg.&lt;g&gt;</filename></term>
				<listitem>
					<para>
						int16, single-channel,
						sample-rate-aligned. The reconstructed
						<literal>EMG_au</literal> trace for group
						<literal>g</literal>, clamped to int16 range.
					</para>
				</listitem>
			</varlistentry>
			<varlistentry>
				<term><filename>basename.res.emg.&lt;g&gt;</filename></term>
				<listitem>
					<para>
						Binary, no header. <literal>nEvents ×
						int64_t</literal> sample-index timestamps
						(little-endian). Same format as
						<filename>basename.res.&lt;g&gt;</filename>.
					</para>
				</listitem>
			</varlistentry>
			<varlistentry>
				<term><filename>basename.spk.emg.&lt;g&gt;</filename></term>
				<listitem>
					<para>
						Binary, no header. <literal>nEvents × nSamples
						× nChannels(g) × int16_t</literal>, sample-major
						layout. Same format as
						<filename>basename.spk.&lt;g&gt;</filename>.
						Waveforms are extracted from the
						<emphasis>original</emphasis>
						<filename>basename.dat</filename>, not the
						cleaned dat.
					</para>
				</listitem>
			</varlistentry>
			<varlistentry>
				<term><filename>basename.emg.meta.yaml</filename></term>
				<listitem>
					<para>
						Sidecar with per-group diagnostics: the
						<literal>loading</literal> (As) and
						<literal>unmixing</literal> (Ws) vectors used,
						the spatial uniformity score of the chosen IC,
						the FastICA iteration count and convergence
						flag, and the threshold and median envelope.
					</para>
				</listitem>
			</varlistentry>
		</variablelist>
	</refsect1>

	<refsect1>
		<title>Algorithm</title>
		<para>
			FastICA is implemented exactly as in
			<filename>fpica.m</filename> case 10 (deflation, pow3):
		</para>
		<screen>for round = 1..K:
    w = randn(nch);  w -= B B' w;  w /= ||w||
    until ||w − wOld|| &lt; ε  OR  ||w + wOld|| &lt; ε:
        w   -= B B' w;  w /= ||w||
        wOld = w
        w    = (Z (Z'w).^3) / N − 3w
        w   /= ||w||
    B(:,round) = w
    A(:,round) = dwm w
    W(round,:) = w' wm</screen>
		<para>
			where <literal>Z</literal> is the whitened input,
			<literal>wm = D^(-1/2) E'</literal> the whitening matrix,
			<literal>dwm = E D^(1/2)</literal> the dewhitening matrix,
			<literal>E, D</literal> the eigenvectors and eigenvalues of
			the channel covariance, and <literal>B</literal> the
			running set of accepted unit vectors. With the toolbox
			defaults: <literal>ε = 1e-4</literal>,
			<literal>maxIter = 1000</literal>, no fine-tuning, no
			stabilisation, full sample size,
			<literal>K = max(round(0.8·nch), min(16, nch))</literal>.
		</para>
		<para>
			The C++ rewrite uses sample-major data storage so the
			pow3 inner kernel reads the whitened data contiguously per
			sample, accumulating into both the projection
			<literal>y[t]</literal> and the back-projection
			<literal>newW[c]</literal> in a single pass. This is
			algorithmically identical to the MATLAB version but
			cache-friendly when N ≫ nch.
		</para>
	</refsect1>

	<refsect1>
		<title>Exit Status</title>
		<variablelist>
			<varlistentry>
				<term>0</term>
				<listitem><para>Success.</para></listitem>
			</varlistentry>
			<varlistentry>
				<term>1</term>
				<listitem>
					<para>
						Error — bad arguments, unreadable input files,
						or I/O failure. Output files are left in their
						previous state on error.
					</para>
				</listitem>
			</varlistentry>
		</variablelist>
	</refsect1>

	<refsect1>
		<title>Examples</title>
		<para>
			Two 4-channel groups, default parameters:
		</para>
		<screen>process_extractemg -n 16 -s 32000 -c 0,1,2,3:8,9,10,11 session</screen>
		<para>
			Verbose, longer ID window, threshold-only run:
		</para>
		<screen>process_extractemg -n 32 -s 30000 -c 0,1,2,3,4,5,6,7 \
                  -B 60 -Z 120 -t 4 -v --no-clean --no-waveforms session</screen>
	</refsect1>

	<refsect1>
		<title>References</title>
		<para>
			Hyvärinen, A. (1999). Fast and robust fixed-point
			algorithms for independent component analysis.
			<emphasis>IEEE Transactions on Neural Networks</emphasis>,
			10(3), 626–634.
		</para>
		<para>
			FastICA Matlab toolbox 2.5,
			<ulink url="http://research.ics.aalto.fi/ica/fastica/">http://research.ics.aalto.fi/ica/fastica/</ulink>.
		</para>
		<para>
			Chen, L. (2019). EMG_removing labbox toolbox.
		</para>
	</refsect1>

	<refsect1>
		<title>See Also</title>
		<para>
			<citerefentry><refentrytitle>ndm_extractemg</refentrytitle><manvolnum>1</manvolnum></citerefentry>,
			<citerefentry><refentrytitle>ndm_extractspikes</refentrytitle><manvolnum>1</manvolnum></citerefentry>,
			<citerefentry><refentrytitle>ndm_hipass</refentrytitle><manvolnum>1</manvolnum></citerefentry>
		</para>
	</refsect1>

	<refsect1>
		<title>Authors</title>
		<para>neurosuite-3 contributors</para>
	</refsect1>

</refentry>
